cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HazardNet, its forecasts or its historical hazard archive in academic work or an operational product, please cite this repository as below."
title: "HazardNet: multi-hazard early warning for Bangladesh agriculture"
abstract: >-
  HazardNet turns satellite, reanalysis and weather-forecast data into 7- and 15-day
  multi-hazard outlooks for the 64 districts of Bangladesh, across eight hazard classes, with a
  dual-track severity (a classification model plus an independent formula-based physics
  cross-check). The work comprises an ingestion and validation ETL, a PostGIS historical event
  store, an MLOps layer (dataset and model registries, calibration, drift verification), a
  human-gated alert engine, and a bilingual, offline-capable public front end that publishes its
  own data provenance and freshness. Master's thesis, Department of Agrometeorology, Bangladesh
  Agricultural University. Supervised by Dr. Ahmed Khairul Hasan; co-supervised by the Department
  of Computer Science and Mathematics, BAU.
type: thesis
